  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education and Training to CITES Authorities in Central America and the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to counter wildlife trafficking in Central America and the Caribbean by capacity development in several countries of the region on the implementation of CITES. This will be done by facilitating the successful selection, mentorship, and graduation of students in a Masters Course on CITES. Key intended results include the graduation of a co- hort of students, and the subsequent strengthening of CITES Authorities in the region.Specific activities will include: (1) facilitating the successful selection, mentorship, and graduation of students on the mentioned Masters Course. A CITES expert will support all academic needs of the students, including contribution to the selection of students among the CITES authorities in the region, support during the in-person stage (11 weeks), support for selection of topics for Master theses and search for directors, and support during the theses elaboration until their completion. (2) coverage of all logistic needs of students: traveling from their countries to Spain and back, accommodation, maintenance, academic taxes, simultaneous interpretation English- Spanish, small economic support for thesis field work, health and accident insurance.</narrative>
  </description>
